# config/Kconfig.packages — signed application packages (plan D14, Phase 6)
#
# crates/core/pkg is the format, the verification and the admission; the
# installer service that runs them is userspace/services/pkgd (USERSPACE_PKGD,
# generated into config/Kconfig.userspace). The device policy that says which
# author keys are admitted is not here: it is the `[signer.NAME]` sections of
# the signed topology (TOPOLOGY_MAX_SIGNERS in config/Kconfig.security).

menu "Application packages"

config PKG_MAX_KB
    int "Largest package the installer accepts (KiB)"
    range 16 65536
    default 4096 if HWCLASS_SERVER
    default 256 if HWCLASS_EMBEDDED
    default 1024
    help
      The installer (PKGD.ELF) reads a package whole into one buffer before it
      verifies a byte of it: the signature covers the metadata, the images are
      checked against the hashes that metadata carries, and the rows are
      parsed only after both. A package larger than this is refused unread.
      The ceiling is also the installer's biggest static buffer.

      Cost: PKG_MAX_KB of RAM in PKGD.ELF (.bss), either ISA; nothing in the
      kernel.

config PKG_META_MAX_KB
    int "Largest manifest or warrant section of a package (KiB)"
    range 1 64
    default 16
    help
      A package carries two small texts besides its images: the metadata
      (name, hardware classes, ABI and interface levels, one hash per image)
      and the rows (the `[task.NAME]` sections that become part of the
      topology). Each is at most this. A larger one is refused before the
      signature is checked.

      Cost: none by itself.

config PKG_MAX_IMAGES
    int "Programs one package may carry"
    range 1 64
    default 8
    help
      Every image of a package is a program with exactly one row, so this is
      also the most rows one package adds to the topology. The metadata parser
      keeps a table of this many images on its stack.

      Cost: 56 B of stack per entry while a package is read, either ISA.

config PKG_MAX_STAGED
    int "Packages staged at once"
    range 1 256
    default 4 if HWCLASS_EMBEDDED
    default 64 if HWCLASS_SERVER
    default 16
    help
      The installer stages a package as one file in /fat/PKG and judges a new
      one against the topology AND the packages already staged (their rows are
      merged first), so it keeps the rows text of each staged package in an
      arena of this many slots of PKG_META_MAX_KB. A package staged beyond
      this is refused (`no room`); remove one first.

      Cost: PKG_MAX_STAGED x PKG_META_MAX_KB of RAM in PKGD.ELF (.bss), either
      ISA; nothing in the kernel.

config PKG_MAX_API
    int "Interface levels one package may require"
    range 1 32
    default 8
    help
      A package states the lowest level it needs of each IDL interface it
      calls (`[api]`). The device refuses it when an interface is missing or
      older. More entries than this are refused by the metadata parser.

      Cost: 24 B of stack per entry while a package is read, either ISA.

endmenu
